{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966786,"nonce":"zVgNMy1CXeboe+ZyzW762gT4zow=","title":"BLINC_DAMAGE_RECT path: text/SVG/image dispatch is now wired (Phase 3.B, commit 1608a571),","message":"The compositor v2 damage-rect path (`render_static_layer_damaged`)\nclears a scissor region of the static cache and re-dispatches every\nSDF primitive in `cached_bg_batch` whose AABB intersects. The\nslow-path equivalent clears the whole cache and dispatches SDF\n**plus** text glyphs + rasterised SVGs + images, all into the same\ntexture.\n\n**Phase 3.A/B (committed)** — `GpuRenderer::pending_scissor` +\ncached `glyphs_by_layer` let the damage path filter cached glyphs\nagainst the union damage rect and re-dispatch via `render_text`\nwith the scissor staged. The \"text wipes\" gap is closed for the\ncommon case.\n\n**Still opt-in only** — the path causes visible animation stutter\nthat the slow path doesn't exhibit, despite both doing comparable\nGPU work. The user repro: cn_demo switch toggle with\n`BLINC_DAMAGE_RECT=1` shows mid-transition jitter; the same toggle\nwithout the flag is smooth. Suspect Metal cost of partial\n`LoadOp::Load` + scissored draw composition vs the slow path's\n`LoadOp::Clear` + full draw, but unconfirmed without GPU profiling\n(Instruments / Metal Frame Capture).\n\n**Things to try when revisiting**:\n- Batch every dispatch in the damage path (clear, SDF, text,\n  composite) into a single command encoder + single submit to\n  reduce GPU sync points.\n- Profile with Metal Frame Capture to see actual GPU pipeline\n  state changes between damage frames.\n- Consider extracting motion-bound primitives from the cache\n  entirely (the \"compositor v2 proper\" cut from purring-juggling-\n  tulip.md) — cache holds static content only, motion-bound\n  elements get a per-frame overlay. Sidesteps the partial-write\n  pattern entirely.\n\nUntil that's done, `BLINC_DAMAGE_RECT` stays default-off. The\ninfrastructure is committed and ready to retry; this isn't a\n\"fresh start\" situation.\n\nSee commits `fb511fdf` (scaffolding) and `1608a571` (Phase 3.B\ntext/SVG/image dispatch).","files":null}]}